<h3><span>A bug report option has been added to the Twine section.</span></h3>
<p>I have some people to thank for this.</p>
<p>Firstly: Thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jakdragonx" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5588260); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5588260&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1579069652" alt="JakdragonX" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5588260)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jakdragonx" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5588260); return false;">JakdragonX</a></span> for getting me back on course with his critique. He made me realize that I had lost the theme of mystery in my earlier drafts.</p>
<p>Secondly: Thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-fullham" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1989312); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1989312&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1579069652" alt="Doctor Fullham" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1989312)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-fullham" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1989312); return false;">Doctor Fullham</a></span> for inspiring me to do the stupid, stupid thing you'll find at the last offset.</p>
<p>Thirdly: Thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-balthazaar" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1468535); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1468535&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1579069652" alt="Dr Balthazaar" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1468535)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-balthazaar" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1468535); return false;">Dr Balthazaar</a></span> for helping me with this. They had no creative input whatsoever, they just helped me with formatting when I had my hand gimped from a car accident.</p>
<p>Fourthly: Thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/captain-kirby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3440103); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3440103&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1579069652" alt="Captain Kirby" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3440103)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/captain-kirby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3440103); return false;">Captain Kirby</a></span> for telling me to reign in my ambition on this.</p>
<p>Fifthly: I have to thank <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kyza" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5565903); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5565903&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1579069652" alt="Kyza" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5565903)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kyza" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5565903); return false;">Kyza</a></span> for helping me get the freakin' hover elements to work.</p>
<p>Lastly: thank you to everyone who agreed to 'die' in the name of this stupid, stupid meta idea.</p>
<p>Actually last but certainly not least: <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/glewmie" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3448977); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3448977&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1579069652" alt="glewmie" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3448977)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/glewmie" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3448977); return false;">glewmie</a></span> was a massive help in helping me learn the basics of Twine. So thanks to them for that.</p>
<p>The Twine file still might have some bugs in it&#8212; if you run into an infinite loop or an error message while it's trying to execute, PM me and I'll get it fixed ASAP.</p>
